            <div xml:id="d378">

                <pb facs="0380" n="264" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg264"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 339.11/16.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister Sullivan.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 69.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-06-22">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 22, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your No. 103
                    of the 3d instant, reporting that your Legation [etc.]</p>
                <p>In reply the Department desires to say that you will endeavor to come to an
                    understanding with the Dominican Government along the lines of the following
                    directions in regard to the drafting of persons claiming to be Porto Ricans:</p>
                <p>The Dominican Government should notify you promptly of any person drafted who
                    claims to be a Porto Rican entitled to American nationality and protection. If
                    it appears, prima facie, that his claim of nationality is well founded, you will
                    request his suspension from service until the question of nationality can be
                    determined by the Department, and to this end you will send to the Department
                    all the evidence obtainable bearing on the matter.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
